# {{ .Name }}

{{ .Description }}

Scaffolded by the [IDP](https://github.com/{{ .Owner }}/idp-backstage). Creating this
repository also applied a `WebApp` custom resource to the cluster, so the service is
already running: the operator reconciled it into a Deployment, a Service and, if
autoscaling was requested, an HPA.

## Endpoints

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/` | Service identity |
| `/healthz` | Liveness: the process is up. Never wire this to a dependency, or a dependency outage becomes a restart loop |
| `/readyz` | Readiness: the process can serve traffic |
| `/metrics` | Prometheus metrics |

## Local development

```bash
make run     # run on :{{ .Port }}
make test
make image   # build the container image
```

## How it gets deployed

Pushing to `{{ .DefaultBranch }}` builds an image and publishes it to
`ghcr.io/{{ .Owner }}/{{ .Name }}` tagged with the commit sha. Point `spec.image` in
[`webapp.yaml`](webapp.yaml) at the new tag and apply it:

```bash
make deploy
```

Tags are always explicit: the operator's admission webhook rejects `:latest` and
untagged images, so an image reference you cannot pin is an image it will not run.
